Description: Put pg_noreturn before the storage-class specifier
 PostgreSQL 19 expands pg_noreturn to [[noreturn]] in C23 mode.
 GCC 15 rejects the attribute between static and the return type.
 Use the declaration order used by the PostgreSQL core.
Author: PGSTY <rh@vonng.com>
Forwarded: no

--- a/contrib/aux_mysql/src/mysql_proto.c
+++ b/contrib/aux_mysql/src/mysql_proto.c
@@ -1081,2 +1081,2 @@
-static pg_noreturn void
+pg_noreturn static void
 mys_auth_failed(Port *port, bool with_password, const char *logdetail)
--- a/contrib/aux_mysql/src/mys_stmt.c
+++ b/contrib/aux_mysql/src/mys_stmt.c
@@ -521,2 +521,2 @@
-static pg_noreturn void
+pg_noreturn static void
 malformed(void)
